  • Aviation Expertise: Leidos' broader Civil
  Division integrates aviation systems,
  modernizes infrastructure, and supports air
  navigation for global providers. LAISI
  handles specific flight operations, such as
  surveys, reconnaissance, and test flights,
  often using aircraft like the Beechcraft
  BE350 or prototypes (e.g., the ARTEMIS
  plane for advanced aerial missions).
  • Government Contracts: LAISI supports
  Leidos' contracts with entities like the U.S.
  Army Geospatial Center and the Nevada
  Test and Training Range (NTTR), involving
  airborne surveys and defense-related
  flights. Examples include operations from
  bases like Offutt AFB and aircraft tracking
  under callsigns like BRIO66.
  This integration allows Leidos to leverage LAISI
  for specialized aviation tasks within its $16 V
